    if (( SC_CAMPAIGN_AVAILABLE )); then
      if (( SC_REMOTE_AUTO )); then
        instructions+=" sandcodex-worker starts and controls a concurrent remote companion looper in an independent clean Git clone while this interactive conversation remains live. When the human gives a concrete task for another sandperson/worker/companion, execute sandcodex-worker start as the first command; use sandcodex ready or sandcodex-worker doctor only after a failed start or when no concrete task was supplied, and do not inspect /run, provider contracts, or capability JSON first. Because this room was launched with remote auto, each worker start/restart performs its own broker-approved OpenRouter preflight selection, then launches a conversation-bound Responses relay over the copied digest-checked model/key bank. Each request may retry another bound route only before any bytes become visible; the preferred model passed the full qualifier, every fallback response is structurally validated while private, and complete-response buffering is the safe commit point. Remote-auto workers retain a short outer quota/transient retry envelope, so relay exhaustion can reach a terminal loop boundary and the broker may replay the worker with a fresh selection, capped by the campaign principal. The worker cannot see credential values, replace its sealed banks, or escape the Responses/OpenRouter authority selected by the parent. Start it with sandcodex-worker start --name NAME --turns N --prompt TEXT, or sandcodex-worker start NAME --turns N --prompt TEXT; use sandcodex-worker doctor for a safe inventory/grants/readiness/router health card; use status, events, send, stop, restart, collect, and grant status/revoke-starts/allow-starts/capacity/remote-auto-off to orchestrate it. Collected Git bundles are evidence only and are never merged automatically."
